.TH SSO\-MIB\-TOOL 1 "2025" "@PACKAGE_NAME@ @PACKAGE_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sso\-mib\-tool \- interact with the Microsoft Identity Broker for SSO on Azure Entra ID
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sso\-mib\-tool
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTION ]...\&
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sso\-mib\-tool
is a command-line frontend to the sso-mib library for interacting with a
Microsoft Identity Broker via DBus. It can be used to list accounts,
acquire authentication tokens (both silently and interactively),
obtain PRT SSO cookies, and generate signed HTTP requests using
Proof-of-Possession (PoP) tokens.
.PP
The tool implements support for the OIDC extension MS-OAPXBC, including
requesting Primary Refresh Tokens and exchanging them for Access Tokens.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B getAccounts
List all accounts registered with the broker. When used with
.BR \-A ,
returns a single account matching the given User Principal Name.
.TP
.B removeAccount
Remove an account from the broker. Use
.B \-a
to specify the account index.
.TP
.B acquirePrtSsoCookie
Acquire a PRT SSO cookie for the selected account. Requires a registered
account. Default scope is
.IR https://graph.microsoft.com/.default .
.TP
.B acquireTokenSilent
Acquire an access token silently (without user interaction) using the
Primary Refresh Token. Requires a registered account.
.TP
.B acquireTokenInteractive
Acquire an access token interactively. This will prompt the user for
authentication via the broker.
.TP
.B getLinuxBrokerVersion
Query and display the version of the Linux identity broker.
.TP
.B generateSignedHttpRequest
Generate a signed HTTP request token for the selected account. Requires
Proof-of-Possession parameters to be specified with
.BR \-P .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-a " index"
Select account by index (default: 0). The account index corresponds to the
position in the list returned by
.BR getAccounts .
.TP
.BI \-A " upn"
Select account by User Principal Name (UPN), e.g.\&
.IR user@example.com .
.TP
.B \-d
Decode JWT tokens in the output. Requires libjwt support at compile time.
.TP
.BI \-f " format"
Set output format. Supported values are
.B text
(default) and
.BR json .
.TP
.B \-h
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-I
Enforce interactive token acquisition, even when a cached token is available.
.TP
.BI \-P " params"
Proof-of-Possession parameters as a JSON string. Required for
.BR generateSignedHttpRequest .
The JSON object supports the following keys:
.RS
.TP
.B authenticationScheme
Either \fB"PoP"\fR or \fB"Bearer"\fR.
.TP
.B resourceRequestMethod
HTTP method: \fB"GET"\fR, \fB"POST"\fR, or \fB"PUT"\fR.
.TP
.B resourceRequestUri
The target resource URI.
.TP
.B shrClaims
(Optional) Additional SHR claims.
.TP
.B shrNonce
(Optional) SHR nonce value.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-r " uri"
OIDC redirect URI for the client application.
.TP
.BI \-s " client_id"
Azure client application ID (default: Microsoft Edge on Linux,
.IR d7b530a4\-7680\-4c23\-a8bf\-c52c121d2e87 ).
.TP
.BI \-S " scope"
OIDC scope to request. This option can be specified multiple times to
request multiple scopes. If not specified, defaults to
.IR https://graph.microsoft.com/.default .
.TP
.BI \-t " token"
Provide a token for renewal (used with
.BR acquireTokenSilent ).
.TP
.BI \-x " authority"
Entra ID (Azure AD) authority URL (default:
.IR https://login.microsoftonline.com/common ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (e.g., no accounts found, invalid parameters, broker
communication failure).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=ssomib
Enable debug logging of DBus call parameters via GLib's message logging system.
.SH EXAMPLES
List all registered accounts:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sso\-mib\-tool getAccounts
.fi
.RE
.PP
Get account details by UPN in JSON format:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sso\-mib\-tool getAccounts \-A user@example.com \-f json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Acquire a token silently with decoded JWT output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sso\-mib\-tool acquireTokenSilent \-d
.fi
.RE
.PP
Acquire a token interactively for SMTP access:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sso\-mib\-tool acquireTokenInteractive \-f json \\
    \-s <client_id> \\
    \-r https://login.microsoftonline.com/common/oauth2/nativeclient \\
    \-x https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant_id> \\
    \-S \(aqhttps://outlook.office365.com/SMTP.Send\(aq
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate a signed HTTP request with PoP parameters:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sso\-mib\-tool generateSignedHttpRequest \\
    \-P \(aq{"authenticationScheme":"PoP","resourceRequestMethod":"POST","resourceRequestUri":"https://example.com/"}\(aq
.fi
.RE
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT
Cancels any in-flight broker operations gracefully.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sso\-mib\-gch\-smtp\-o365 (1)
.SH AUTHORS
@PACKAGE_AUTHORS@
